From: book4-edge-linux
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: samsung-emuec: let the firmware negotiate before requesting a PD contract (experiment)

On top of patches/0001-0003. Plugged in while the system sleeps, a charger
gets its 20 V contract from the PD firmware alone and the battery charges
(58 -> 99 % overnight). Plugged in while awake, the driver requested within
milliseconds, the S2MM006 had not settled, the request timed out (-110),
the port sat at 5 V and the retry reached 20 V a second later; the battery
then charged at ~1 W, apparently because the EC keeps the input limit it
set for 5 V (docs/power.md, 6-7 October).

After a new attach, wait pd_grace_ms (default 3000, runtime-writable in
/sys/module/samsung_emuec/parameters, 0 = old behaviour) and request only
if the contract is still below the best fixed PDO. Resume and the sleep
handling of 0002/0003 do not start a new attach, so they are unchanged.

Untested, not compiled.

---
--- a/samsung-emuec.c	2026-10-07 14:11:16.032862017 +0200
+++ b/samsung-emuec.c	2026-10-07 14:11:30.694044376 +0200
@@ -109,6 +109,7 @@
 	struct notifier_block pm_nb;
 	bool quiesced;
 	bool wake_armed;
+	unsigned long attach_time;
 };
 
 static int samsung_emuec_pm_notify(struct notifier_block *nb,
@@ -397,6 +398,20 @@
 	return -ETIMEDOUT;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A charger plugged in while the system sleeps has its 20 V contract
+ * negotiated by the PD firmware on its own, and the battery charges. Plugged
+ * in while awake, the request below went out before the S2MM006 had settled,
+ * timed out, the port sat at 5 V and only the retry reached 20 V; the
+ * battery then got ~1 W (the EC appears to keep the 5 V input limit). Give
+ * the firmware this long after an attach before requesting anything.
+ * 0 restores the old behaviour. Only a new attach waits: resume and the
+ * sleep handling do not go through here with a fresh attach_time.
+ */
+static unsigned int pd_grace_ms = 3000;
+module_param(pd_grace_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(pd_grace_ms, "ms after a charger attach before the driver requests a PD contract (0: at once)");
+
 static void samsung_emuec_update_pd(struct samsung_emuec *pdic)
 {
 	struct usb_power_delivery_capabilities_desc caps = { .role = TYPEC_SOURCE };
@@ -459,7 +474,12 @@
 		 * has settled and time out; it succeeds when repeated a little
 		 * later, so retry a few times instead of staying at 5 V.
 		 */
-		if (pdic->pd_attempts < 5) {
+		unsigned long due = pdic->attach_time + msecs_to_jiffies(pd_grace_ms);
+
+		if (pd_grace_ms && time_before(jiffies, due)) {
+			/* Let the firmware negotiate first; look again at the deadline. */
+			mod_delayed_work(system_dfl_wq, &pdic->work, due - jiffies);
+		} else if (pdic->pd_attempts < 5) {
 			pdic->pd_attempts++;
 			ret = samsung_emuec_request_pdo(pdic, requested);
 			if (ret) {
@@ -857,6 +877,7 @@
 		}
 
 		pdic->attached = true;
+		pdic->attach_time = jiffies;
 		pdic->power_role = power_role;
 		pdic->data_role = data_role;
 		typec_port_set_usb_mode(pdic->port, USB_MODE_NONE);
